<title>SOUTH AFRICA: HCI yr shr down, withdraws cautionary.</title>
<headline>HCI yr shr down, withdraws cautionary.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre non-recurring   11.0	  vs 19.6</p>
<p>    - post non-recurring  39.3	  vs 86.1</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   28.91	 vs 18.24</p>
<p>Income before non-recurring items</p>
<p>				  8.12 profit vs 4.61 loss</p>
<p>    Non-recurring items   20.80 gain  vs 22.40 gain</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   1.76	  vs 0.92</p>
<p>    Turnover		  23.88	 vs nil</p>
<p>Full name: Hosken Consolidated Investments Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said that the results were not indicative of the group's expected performance in the year ahead as it now owned stakes in firms which should prosper. These businesses were active in cellular telephony, radio, mining and video sectors.</p>
<p>The group would seek opportunities to grow its capital base, focusing on financial services, gaming, media and information technology areas.</p>
<p>Shareholders were advised that talks referred to in earlier cautionaries had not been successful.</p>
<p>During the year the number of shares in issue increased vastly following a rights issue to raise 186 million rand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
